{
  "case_id": "2017-16-969",
  "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory A. Castanias",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For three reasons, the Patent Trial and Appeal Board is not authorized to issue final written decisions on fewer than all of the patent claims challenged by inter partes review petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 16-969, SAS Institute versus Matal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm not at all clear what it is you're challenging here. Are you challenging the Board's right to initiate partial adjudications or are you challenging the fact that they are not addressing all of the claims in their final decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory A. Castanias",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it's an if/then. It's a binary, that if it's instituted, then we're entitled to a decision on all challenged patent claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Patent Office in this case, the\nBoard, decided to institute review with respect\nto claim 4, but not claim 2."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOND: It issued a lengthy decision, about half as long as the final decision, but they're different in kind."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: What do you say about our -- our last argument, where a lot of our attention focused on Congress's putative intention to -- to want to move things to an expert agency and -- and speed things along"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0002-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It would be highly incongruous for Congress to say, when the expert agency is reviewing patents it has issued, it lacks discretion to constrain the scope of its review and lacks discretion to do what is ordinarily the rule in patent law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner Gregory A. Castanias",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have three specific responses to points made by my friend and then four broader points that I hope I'll be able to get in in my limited time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You talked about canceled claims. How about settled claims? Say, in the middle of the proceedings, you settle a claim. Under your theory, the Board would still have to address that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "-- is what language says that partial institution is not permissible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-969",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "30db097e9f01d2ed9928331ffe951063865d975a880c6e8a75e4aff5fd5dee7f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-30db097e9f01-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
